  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Prime stretch of Fall weather continues today and\nSaturday. \n\nHigh pressure remains in control of our weather and will\ncontinue to deliver dry conditions for Friday and Saturday.\nAfter some patchy valley fog this morning, mostly sunny skies\nwill slowly give way to increasing clouds later this evening. \nThere could be quite a picturesque sunset tonight. Saturday will\nbe similar temperatures to today (mid 60s to low 70s) but much \nmore cloudy. High clouds streaming in ahead of Isaias will\nfilter the sunshine and be accompanied by gradually lowering\ncloud bases Saturday afternoon and evening.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Rain and breezy conditions from Isaias arrive\nSaturday night and continue on Sunday. \n\nThe northeast edge of Isaias' rain shield will arrive in\nsouthwest PA Saturday evening and lift northeast through Sunday\nmorning. The heaviest rainfall is expected to occur early Sunday\nmorning and then give way to scattered rain showers through the\nrest of the day and overnight .Total rainfall amounts are \ngenerally forecast in the 0.50-1.50 inch range over a 24-36hr \nduration with a low risk of potential flooding impacts. A tight\npressure gradient around Isaias's weakening remnants will\ndeliver wind gusts 35-40 mph over the ridgetops in the Laurel \nHighlands on Sunday.",
